1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:19,475
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June fifteenth. Japan played its first match at the World Cup, against one of the strongest teams in the world, the Netherlands — and came from behind twice to earn a hard-fought draw. Let's listen.

2
00:00:20,076 --> 00:00:22,835
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:23,536 --> 00:00:31,288
[News] サッカーのワールドカップが始まり、日本代表が初めての試合をしました。

4
00:00:31,987 --> 00:00:39,356
[News] 6月15日、日本は、強い相手のオランダと戦いました。

5
00:00:40,055 --> 00:00:44,543
[News] 試合は、2対2の引き分けでした。

6
00:00:45,243 --> 00:00:52,468
[News] 日本は、2回も先に点を取られましたが、あきらめませんでした。

7
00:00:53,167 --> 00:01:00,055
[News] 後半、中村選手が1点を返して、同点にしました。

8
00:01:00,756 --> 00:01:08,628
[News] 試合の終わりごろ、鎌田選手がゴールを決めて、もう一度追いつきました。

9
00:01:09,328 --> 00:01:15,808
[News] この引き分けで、日本は大切な勝ち点を1つ取りました。

10
00:01:16,507 --> 00:01:23,108
[News] 試合の途中、久保選手はけがをして、交代しました。

11
00:01:23,808 --> 00:01:32,280
[News] 森保監督は、「チーム全員で、最後まで戦いました」と話しました。

12
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:34,611
[Host] Let's break it down.

13
00:01:35,212 --> 00:01:44,091
[Slow] サッカーのワールドカップが始まり、日本代表が初めての試合をしました。

14
00:01:44,891 --> 00:01:50,819
[Host] The soccer World Cup began, and Japan's national team played its first match.

15
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:53,772
[Vocab] 代表

16
00:01:54,171 --> 00:02:02,572
[Host] It means representative — and for a country's sports team, it means the national team. The players who represent the whole country.

17
00:02:03,171 --> 00:02:11,596
[Slow] 6月15日、日本は、強い相手のオランダと戦いました。

18
00:02:12,395 --> 00:02:17,651
[Host] On June fifteenth, Japan played against a strong opponent, the Netherlands.

19
00:02:18,252 --> 00:02:20,340
[Vocab] 相手

20
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:28,683
[Host] It means the other side — an opponent, or a partner in conversation. Who you're facing, whether in a game or a chat.

21
00:02:29,283 --> 00:02:34,419
[Slow] 試合は、2対2の引き分けでした。

22
00:02:35,219 --> 00:02:37,548
[Host] The match was a two-to-two draw.

23
00:02:38,147 --> 00:02:40,548
[Vocab] 引き分け

24
00:02:40,948 --> 00:02:48,556
[Host] It means a draw, a tie — when neither side wins. It comes from pulling evenly, both sides level.

25
00:02:49,156 --> 00:02:57,412
[Slow] 日本は、2回も先に点を取られましたが、あきらめませんでした。

26
00:02:58,211 --> 00:03:01,716
[Host] Japan fell behind twice, but didn't give up.

27
00:03:02,316 --> 00:03:04,812
[Vocab] あきらめる

28
00:03:05,211 --> 00:03:12,243
[Host] It means to give up, to quit trying. Here it's negative — they did not give up, and that's how they earned the draw.

29
00:03:12,843 --> 00:03:20,716
[Slow] 後半、中村選手が1点を返して、同点にしました。

30
00:03:21,515 --> 00:03:26,508
[Host] In the second half, player Nakamura got a goal back and tied the score.

31
00:03:27,108 --> 00:03:29,364
[Vocab] 同点

32
00:03:29,764 --> 00:03:38,451
[Host] It means a tied score, level on points. The first character means same, the second means point — same number of points.

33
00:03:39,051 --> 00:03:48,051
[Slow] 試合の終わりごろ、鎌田選手がゴールを決めて、もう一度追いつきました。

34
00:03:48,852 --> 00:03:54,804
[Host] Near the end of the match, player Kamada scored a goal and drew level once again.

35
00:03:55,403 --> 00:03:57,539
[Vocab] 決める

36
00:03:57,939 --> 00:04:04,587
[Host] It means to decide — and in sports, to score a goal cleanly. To get a goal in is to decide it.

37
00:04:05,187 --> 00:04:12,580
[Slow] この引き分けで、日本は大切な勝ち点を1つ取りました。

38
00:04:13,379 --> 00:04:18,108
[Host] With this draw, Japan earned one valuable point in the standings.

39
00:04:18,708 --> 00:04:20,963
[Vocab] 勝ち点

40
00:04:21,363 --> 00:04:29,475
[Host] It means a point in the standings — the points a team earns from wins and draws. A win gives three, a draw gives one.

41
00:04:30,076 --> 00:04:37,636
[Slow] 試合の途中、久保選手はけがをして、交代しました。

42
00:04:38,435 --> 00:04:42,779
[Host] During the match, player Kubo got injured and was substituted.

43
00:04:43,379 --> 00:04:45,636
[Vocab] 交代

44
00:04:46,036 --> 00:04:52,564
[Host] It means a substitution, a changing of places. One player comes off and another comes on.

45
00:04:53,163 --> 00:04:56,163
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

46
00:04:56,764 --> 00:04:59,524
[News] 今日のニュースです。

